> Amulets
>  v - an uncursed amulet of reflection (being worn)
>  L - the blessed Eye of the Aethiopica

Good way to go, reflection is (usually) more valueable than ESP.

>  Armor
>  a - an uncursed +3 pair of leather gloves (being worn)
>  b - an uncursed greased +4 robe (being worn)
>  n - a blessed +5 small shield (being worn)
>  o - a +2 elven leather helm (being worn)
>  N - a +4 pair of boots called jumping boots (being worn)
>  P - a +0 Hawaiian shirt (being worn)

Remember to dis-equip things you don't want enchanted before enchanting
armour.  You don't want to lose your boots, robe, or shield to
over-enchantment.

>  Potions
> h - a golden potion
>  X - a potion of full healing

Do you have the identify spell?  If you do, use it early and often.

>  Rings
>  J - an uncursed +2 ring of increase damage
>  Q - an uncursed ring of free action (on right hand)

I'd wear them both (at least when there are nasties about).  Unless you
plan on lolly-gaging about, the increase damage bonus is more than
worth it.

IIRC, you have a 2nd ring (somewhere), so I'd probably try to charge
one of them higher.

>  Tools
>  e - a greased bag named LOOK MORE STUFF IN HERE
>  g - a +0 unicorn horn
>  m - a magic marker

I'd ID those marker charges and bless that unihorn (be sure to keep a
!holy water on tap).

You don't need to wish for charging scrolls.  You already know (based
on your OP) how to write them.  You just need some blank scrolls.
Hopefully the RNG has been generous enough to provide you with some
worth of blanking.  A blessed magic marker would be a better wish.
Even if you get a bad one (0:30), you can get 2xb?charging out of it
(plus change, possibly enough for another useful scroll) before
recharging it.

> Should I go and poke around the upper Quest levels before I take on
> Gehennom?

I'd explore the Valley of the Dead before tackling the upper quest
levels.  If you're still not comfortable, map some of the upper levels
of Gehennom before tackling the 2nd half of the quest.  You'll need to
bless your unihorn before you can safely tackle Gehennom (down to Orcus
town) in (relative) safety.  A pick-axe is also useful (for digging
paths in the mazes).

